From: Codex <codex@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 15:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: fix bFLT R32 relocation byte order

The 0100 device log reached later BusyBox relocations and failed on an R32
entry at 0x87ed0. The file contains the valid pointer value 0x000021d4 there,
but binfmt_flat logged 0xd4210000 because the MIPS helper returned the raw
little-endian word while the generic non-GOTPIC path applies ntohl().

Return R32 values in the same encoded form as the R26 and HI16/LO16 helpers so
the generic bFLT relocation path sees the intended target address.
---
 arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h b/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
index f319586..55435a4 100644
--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
@@ -184,6 +184,9 @@ static inline int flat_get_addr_from_rp(u32 __user *rp, u32 relval, u32 flags,
 	u32 __user *hi_rp;
 
 	switch (flat_mips_reloc_type(relval)) {
+	case FLAT_MIPS_R_32:
+		*addr = htonl(get_unaligned(p));
+		return 0;
 	case FLAT_MIPS_R_26:
 		insn = get_unaligned(p);
 		*addr = htonl((insn & 0x03ffffff) << 2);
-- 
